Description: link media2 and libbe's ColumnListView, not media and columnlistview
 V\OS ships the media kit as libmedia2.so (the media2 headers keep the
 legacy file and class names), so -lmedia fails at link time; and
 ColumnListView lives inside libbe (src/kits/interface/ColumnListView.cpp),
 no libcolumnlistview.so exists anywhere, so -lcolumnlistview fails too.
 The application and the BeEncoder add-on both lose 'media' in favour of
 'media2', and the application loses 'columnlistview'.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/Hare

--- a/Makefile_Hare
+++ b/Makefile_Hare
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@
 #	- 	if your library does not follow the standard library naming scheme,
 #		you need to specify the path to the library and it's name.
 #		(e.g. for mylib.a, specify "mylib.a" or "path/mylib.a")
-LIBS = $(STDCPPLIBS) hare tag be game media tracker columnlistview
+LIBS = $(STDCPPLIBS) hare tag be game media2 tracker
 
 #	Specify additional paths to directories following the standard libXXX.so
 #	or libXXX.a naming scheme. You can specify full paths or paths relative
--- a/src/Encoders/BeEncoder/Makefile
+++ b/src/Encoders/BeEncoder/Makefile
@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@
 #	- 	if your library does not follow the standard library naming scheme,
 #		you need to specify the path to the library and it's name.
 #		(e.g. for mylib.a, specify "mylib.a" or "path/mylib.a")
-LIBS = hare tag be media
+LIBS = hare tag be media2
 
 #	Specify additional paths to directories following the standard libXXX.so
 #	or libXXX.a naming scheme. You can specify full paths or paths relative
